Article 4 (Terms of Office of Members, etc.)
(1) The term of office of a commissioned member shall be two years: Provided, That where the Committee is dissolved pursuant to Article 5, the member's term shall expire at the time of dissolution. <Amended on December 9, 2025>
(2) Even after the term under paragraph (1) expires, a commissioned member may continue to perform duties until a successor is commissioned. <Newly inserted on December 9, 2025>
(3) The President may remove a commissioned member from office where that member falls under any of the following: <Newly inserted on December 9, 2025>
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform duties due to physical or mental weakness or other reasons;
2. Where the member has engaged in misconduct in connection with official duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unsuitable to remain a member due to neglect of duty, conduct detrimental to dignity, or other reasons;
4. Where the member expresses an intention that he or she has difficulty performing the duties.
